From: open-3d-memory-chipflow maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] drt: consider down vias for standard-cell pins at top layer

TaiWei-Pin-3D mirrors the upper tier, placing upper-tier standard-cell pins
on M1_m at the top of the unified routing stack. FlexPA historically tries a
DOWN via only for IO terminals, so six ordinary upper-tier input pins in the
ASAP7 GCD case have no access point even though VIA12_m connects M1_m to M2_m.

Keep the existing IO behavior and also consider the adjacent DOWN via when a
pin layer has no routing layer above it. This does not disable pin access or
relax any DRC rule.
---
 src/drt/src/pa/FlexPA_acc_point.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/drt/src/pa/FlexPA_acc_point.cpp b/src/drt/src/pa/FlexPA_acc_point.cpp
index d146df97e0..051c5ad788 100644
--- a/src/drt/src/pa/FlexPA_acc_point.cpp
+++ b/src/drt/src/pa/FlexPA_acc_point.cpp
@@ -908,3 +908,6 @@ void FlexPA::filterViaAccess(
-    // DOWN Vias
-    if (isIOTerm(inst_term)) {
+    // Mirrored 3D stacks can place standard-cell pins on the top routing
+    // layer. There is no UP via in that case, so also consider the adjacent
+    // DOWN via instead of rejecting every access point for the pin.
+    if (isIOTerm(inst_term)
+        || layer_num + 1 > router_cfg_->TOP_ROUTING_LAYER) {
       collect_vias(layer_num - 1, max_num_via_trial);
